## Question 13: Monte Carlo Fn estimator 

$$
F_X(x)= P(X \leq x) = \mathbb{E}[1_{X \leq x}] 
$$
The Monte Carlo estimator is: 

$$
\frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n 1_{X_i \leq x}
$$
## Question 14: strong consistency of Fn(x)

$(1_{X_i \leq x})_{i=1}^n $ are i.i.d variables

$$\forall i \in \{1, \dots, n\}, \quad 1_{X_i \leq x} \sim \text{Ber}(p), \text{ where } p = P(X \leq x) = F_X(x)$$

The law of large numbers gives that 

$$F_n(x) = \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n 1_{X_i \leq x} \xrightarrow{\text{a.s.}}_{n \to \infty} \mathbb{E}[1_{X_i \leq x}] = F_X(x)$$

So F_n(x) is a strong consistent estimator of $F_X(x)$. 


