## Question 16 

Let $(Y_i)_{i=1}^n$ be $n$ i.i.d square integrable random variables.

The central limit theorem states that:

$$
\sqrt{n} \left( \overline{Y_n} - \mathbb{E}[Y_i] \right) \xrightarrow{d}_{n \to \infty} \mathcal{N}(0, \text{Var}(Y_1))
$$
Here we apply the CLT to $Y_i = 1_{X_i \leq x}$.

We know that $1_{X_i \leq x} \overset{\text{iid}}{\sim} \text{Ber}(p)$, where $p = F_X(x)$.

$$
\sqrt{n} \left( \frac{1}{n} \sum_{i=1}^n 1_{X_i \leq x} - \mathbb{E}[1_{X_i \leq x}] \right) \xrightarrow{D}_{n \to \infty} \mathcal{N}(0, \text{Var}(1_{X_i \leq x}))
$$

$$
\Rightarrow \quad \sqrt{n} \left( F_n(x) - F_X(x) \right) \xrightarrow{D}_{n \to \infty} \mathcal{N}(0, p(1-p))
$$

$$
\Rightarrow \quad \sqrt{n} \frac{F_n(x) - F_X(x)}{\sqrt{p(1-p)}} \xrightarrow{D}_{n \to \infty} \mathcal{N}(0, 1)
$$

$$
\text{CI}_{95\%} = \left[ F_n(x) \pm \frac{q_{0.975} \cdot \sqrt{F_n(x) (1 - F_n(x))}}{\sqrt{n}} \right]
$$
where $q_{0.975}$ is the quantile of $N(0,1)$ of order 0.975. 


